  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Colour-Coded Switchboard",
    "overview": "slop-term is a panel for many hosts at once. The chrome is grey and stays still. Colour is how you tell hosts apart: each Session can carry one of eight Session colours, and that colour tints the terminal, the header bar and the SFTP pane. Everything else is neutral, so a coloured Tab is the loudest thing on screen.\n\nThe look is compact. Rows are 22px, text is 13px, and borders are 1px. The user lives in this window all day, so density and speed come before decoration. The palette is GitHub Primer, in a light and a dark mode that follow the operating system or a setting.\n\nConfirmed rejection: the app must not feel like a website. No large rounded cards, big padding or web-style toasts.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Grey chrome, with colour reserved for Session colours and for state (error, warning, success).",
      "Dense rows (22px) and small text (11 to 13px).",
      "Flat at rest. Shadows only on layers that float above the window.",
      "Light and dark modes use one token set, switched by `light-dark()`.",
      "No Tab strip. Open Tabs are listed in the tree under their Saved session."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Session Colour Rule",
        "body": "Session colours are the only decorative colour. Chrome never uses a hue for style alone.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The State Colour Rule",
        "body": "Red means error or destructive, amber means warning, green means success or the main action. Do not reuse them as decoration.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Contrast Rule",
        "body": "Text over a Session colour is black or white, whichever contrasts more. Dimming is not applied there, so the contrast floor holds.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Rule",
        "body": "Sizes, times and counts use `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` so columns line up.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat-At-Rest Rule",
        "body": "Nothing carries a shadow until it floats above other content.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep chrome neutral and let the Session colour be the loudest colour in the window.",
      "Do use 22px rows, 13px text and 1px borders for new list and form screens.",
      "Do take every colour from the tokens above, using `var(--name)` so light and dark both work.",
      "Do put one green primary button in a dialog and make danger actions red only when destructive.",
      "Do show hover-only controls (like the row `+`) on keyboard focus as well.",
